    {
      "name": "propose_roadmap_change",
      "description": "Propose one to 100 changes to one roadmap. Nothing is written until the person reviews the proposal and applies it, and a newer proposal replaces the one waiting on this roadmap. Changes apply in order. A field that names a step or a kind takes its id, or the `ref` an earlier change gave a new one. Each op takes exactly these fields:\nadd_step: required ref, label; optional description, kind, prerequisites, links. Without kind the step takes terracotta.\nremove_step: required nodeId; optional none. The steps after it follow its own prerequisites.\nrename: required nodeId, label; optional none.\ndescribe: required nodeId; optional description, links. Send at least one; each replaces the step's whole value, so to add one web link send every link it is to carry.\nset_kind: required nodeId, kind; optional none.\nconnect: required nodeId, prerequisiteId; optional none. The step nodeId comes to wait on prerequisiteId.\ndisconnect: required nodeId, prerequisiteId; optional none. The step nodeId stops waiting on prerequisiteId.\nmerge: required nodeId, removeId; optional label, description. removeId folds into nodeId, which keeps its mark and web links: the prerequisite links into and out of removeId move to nodeId, and removeId's web links go with it.\nsplit: required nodeId, parts; optional none. Two or more parts, each with a ref and a label and, if wanted, a description, a kind and links. Each part follows the old step's prerequisites, precedes what it unlocked, and takes its mark and, unless it names one, its kind.\nset_progress: required nodeId, status; optional none.\nadd_kind: required ref, label, hue; optional description. A hue another kind wears is refused.\nrename_kind: required kind, label; optional none.\nrecolor_kind: required kind, hue; optional none. The steps that wear its hue take the new one. A hue another kind wears is refused, so two kinds cannot swap hues.\nThe answer names each step the proposal removes, with what it holds.",
